  "parity": "Info now reuses the width just measured when its hybrid labels match, and adjusts the current render list in place. In 60 modeled width changes, the usual FPS and ping row uses 120 width queries instead of 240. The dense row uses 2,010 instead of 2,220. The item-level and GearScore case keeps all 960 queries because the labels change. The decorative slot skips 120 grid-height reads over 60 crossings. Text, fonts, anchors, tooltip contents and slot visibility match.",
  "rules": "The horizontal layout owns its render list for one synchronous pass. It reuses the measured width only with the same glyph text, FontStrings and font size. Changed labels, including compact-to-full and restricted values, keep measurement. The real Info frame keeps its height writes and stat refreshes. A decorative gap follows its top and bottom anchors directly without sampling unused grid heights.",
